inion as  foreigner did I played the hell out of  foreigner I was drawn in by the medieval  combat and I got my first real taste of  why fighting games must be so much fun  at its best Verona requires you to look  for patterns in your enemy's playstyle  and then predict and punish them  accordingly  the skill cap in this game was huge to  the point where the best players would  focus on one character and attempt to  play every match up perfectly the  problem was most of the cast of  characters were blatantly underpowered  and good characters like warden or  warlord were good because they had a  couple of risk free almost unpunished  ball attacks months went by and nothing  changed the community clamored for  tweaks and wrote a ton of really good  suggestions but to this day I'm pretty  sure the game still has a lot of the  same problems they did at launch it  rewards players who play super defensive  and it encourages you to buy the DLC  characters who actually have developed  movesets  they created something really unique and  special with fauna but I'll be much more  cautious about falling in love with fur  on a--to and so my personal game of the  year the game that's given me the most  fun the most wholesome feeling of  community apart from souls and the most  hope for the future is Gwent The Witcher  card game as of the release of this  video quent will have just received a  100 card expansion and  a ton of visual upgrades to animations  and the UI if you're looking for a time  to get into this game now is the time  because there's also a Christmas deal on  packs if you did want to get a head  start on your collection and as I've  mentioned this is a good dev team that  worth supporting in early 2018 we'll  also be receiving the single player  throne breaker campaign which appears to  have this mixture of story deck building  exploration and of course playing the  actual game this game has got better  with every patch and I think it's  something worth keeping an eye on if  this is what you're into in the  description I've listed a bunch of Handy  Gwent guides Gwent streamers and decks  to help you try and get started it's not  as easy as some of the card games on the  market but it is well worth your time so  please vote in the poll down below and  Merry Christmas everybody


